<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea sells dlrs at 857.00 to support won.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea sells dlrs at 857.00 to support won.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea was seen selling dollars at 857.00 won in Friday morning trading to slow the U.S. unit's climb against the domestic currency, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank refused to comment on talk of its intervention in the interbank market.</p>
<p>The won rebounded to 856.40 shortly following the intervention, from its morning low of 857.00.</p>
<p>It had opened the day's trading at 854.00, after closing on Thursday at 854.90.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
